These are the files for the Life with David, Bare Metal Adventures, Chapter 19: Compiling and running Microsoft's m6502 BASIC on an RP2040. 
https://youtu.be/lKHKttM7v0Y
They include: 
  The original Microsoft source program (m6502.asm) with original depricated syntax
  The m6502 BASIC with updated ca65 syntax (Pico_TIM_m6502.asm)
  The ca65 configuration file (ptim_m6502_ld65.cfg)
  A makefile for the ca65 compiling process (makefile)
  The TIM monitor for the emulated 6502 (Pico_TIM.asm)
  A Python program for converting numbers preceded with "@" from octal to hexadecimal (octal_conv.py)
  ***The above programs should be located in a separate directory to create the emu_prog.prg file that is then copied into the 
    main project director.  Other programs, such as ca65.exe, da65.exe, ld65.exe, and srec_cat.exe should also be located in 
    this directory.
  *** The following files should be located in the main project directory:
  The RP2040 6502 emulator (assembly.S)
  The PIO program for the RP2040 keyboard scanning (kb_scan_decode.pio)
  The keyboard and display program for Blinken (kbDisplayIntegrated.c)
  The linker file for the emulator (memmap_staged.LD)
  The startup file for Blinken (startup.c)
  The SSD1306 font file for Blinken (ssd1306_font.h)
  The CMakeLists file for Blinken (CMakeLists.txt)
See BMA, Chapter 18 for more info on compiling and running Blinken:  
Also included is a .uf2 file of the entire emulator, Blinken interface, TIM, and m6502 BASIC
  if you don't want to go through the compilation process (BMA19_m6502.uf2)
